Also contains, unrelated to the subject line: four more CV templates and the
generator axes they needed.

  Elegant   Times, centred head, photo above the name, wide margins.
  Akzent    a coloured band across the top, photo set on it, quiet columns under.
  Schlicht  no colour and no rules; the headings are carried by tracking alone.
  Chronik   a hairline down the column with a dot at each station.

Files: cv-themes.js (the four themes and the preview that draws them), app.js
(font whitelist, band header, centred header, plain headings with tracking, the
timeline, and the Einspaltig/Zweispaltig badge in the picker), test.js (five
tests under "CV templates").

Chronik does NOT set the dates in a column of their own — the shape 14a55f7 had
to defend against. A text extractor reads columns one after another, so dates set
beside their entries arrive detached and get paired by order, stamping entries
with dates the candidate never wrote. The timeline here is a rule and a dot and
carries no text at all.

One bug fixed with it: write() and bulletList() decided which column a line
belonged to by asking whether x equalled MAIN_X. That held while every
main-column line began exactly at the column; an entry indented past a timeline
begins after it, and would have advanced the rail's cursor instead.

This landed here because two sessions were committing to the branch at once. The
split-out version of this work is preserved on the local branch
split-cv-from-jobs (75e4673), whose tree is identical to ad7347d.
